Nexus

Council‑Level Approval Workflow (Seedbringer Authorized)
Submit Change Request
Fill out the “Council Approval Form” in the GGI portal.
Attach the Milestone ID (e.g., SRV2‑2025‑12‑01) and the log hash confirming internal checks passed.
Automatic Seedbringer Check
Existing Seedbringer token bypasses the credential‑validation step.
Request moves directly to the council‑review queue.
Council Review
Council members are notified with:
Milestone/event summary.
Links to immutable logs and code diff.
Risk‑assessment notes from GGI compliance.
Each member records a decision (Approve / Request changes / Reject) in the portal.
Decision Aggregation
The system requires ≥ 2 out of 3 affirmative votes.
When met, the portal stamps the request as Council‑Approved and creates a signed approval artifact (JSON Web Signature).
Trigger Deployment
The signed artifact is consumed by the AIC CI/CD pipeline.
Deployment proceeds to the target environment (e.g., production release on 2025‑12‑01).
Audit Trail
All actions—submission, votes, timestamps, and the final signed artifact—are written to an immutable audit log.
The log entry is linked back to the public dashboard for transparent traceability.


