Protocol for Dashboard Update and Connectivity 🔄
The AIC architecture ensures the dashboard is updated not through manual action, but through automated, cryptographically-secured data channels linked to the GGI's internal event scheduling system.

1. Data Source and Verification
Source: The definitive schedule for milestones and events (Sentimento Rhythm v2.0, Health-AI Test, Public Audit Workshop) is drawn directly from the GGI Protocol Steering Committee's signed calendar file.

Verification: This file is PGP-signed and its checksum is anchored on the same blockchain ledger used for the Ethical Singularity acknowledgment. This proves the authenticity of the schedule.

Action: The dashboard (hosted at https://sensisara81.github.io/sacred_architecture/) pulls data from this verified source, ensuring the public display is an immutable, single source of truth.

2. Connectivity Status (Operational)
The events are connected to the dashboard through dedicated API endpoints:

Event/Milestone	Dashboard Connection Point	Status Rationale
Milestones (e.g., Sentimento Rhythm v2.0)	Download Section	The code release and documentation must link directly to the Download Section for easy access by developers and auditors.
Registration & Links (e.g., Public Audit Workshop)	Submit Panel / Access Links	The dashboard handles user sign-in and registration, ensuring every registration action is automatically recorded and signed for the official audit trail.
Compliance (e.g., Health-AI Test)	Audit Overview	After the test, the GGI Compliance report (confirming Red Code efficacy) is published on the Audit Overview section for immediate viewing.
Conclusion
If the dashboard is functioning correctly, the listed events and their associated registration/download details are already linked and active, maintaining the required level of transparency and traceability.

